fact WorkItem(id: "WI-298", description: some(value: "Rule-occurrence opener: remap DeBruijn vars inside the REMAINING TermId fields after the param lift (open_debruijn_node / substitute_occurrence), AND make the remaining occurrence walkers symmetric with node_to_debruijn for Pattern-kind occurrences. PROBLEM (WI-296 code-review finding 3): open_debruijn_node and substitute_occurrence walk only Rc<NodeOccurrence> children via for_each_child + reassemble; several TermId-typed fields hold materialized terms with DeBruijn vars that are NOT remapped to fresh Globals — diverging from the term-level term_from_debruijn (which remaps all subterms). LATENT today: SLD matching uses the TERM body (patterns remapped correctly there); the occurrence view's un-remapped fields only bite once the typer/simp READS them (typing rules over rule occurrences, WI-079). SCOPE AFTER WI-319 (Pattern reform): WI-319 lifts Lambda.param / LambdaWithin.param / Let.pattern / MatchBranch.pattern from TermId to Rc<NodeOccurrence>(NodeKind::Pattern). WI-298's residual scope is now: (1) Let.type_annotation: Option<TermId>; (2) Expr::Apply.type_args / Expr::ApplyWithin.type_args: Vec<(Option<Symbol>, TermId)>. Plus, NEW from WI-319 code-review (deferred fixes): (3) extend the Pattern-kind descent to the OTHER walkers that don't yet recurse into Pattern children — collect_occurrence_global_vars_ordered (node_occurrence.rs ~1188), collect_occurrence_global_vars, occurrence_has_unbound_var, collect_occurrence_type_constraints (typing.rs ~7215), collect_unbound_vars_node (resolve.rs ~2721), (try_)occurrence_to_term (node_occurrence.rs ~1297). Latent today because Pattern.Var.type_ann is always None at load_pattern_var (load.rs:4963), but the slot is in the public Pattern enum API and any future pass writing to it (proposal 035 lambda binder annotations; reflection-synthesized patterns) silently undercounts/skips vars. REQUIRES: thread kb (term store) into open_debruijn_node + reassemble + their callers (open_debruijn_node currently has no kb), then remap those TermIds via KnowledgeBase::term_from_debruijn (mod.rs:1938) — mirroring the closing-side node_to_debruijn. ACCEPTANCE: a rule whose body has a let with a type annotation referencing ?p (or an Apply type_arg referencing ?p) shows the bound var in the occurrence view remapped to the same Global as the body's ?p; all listed walkers descend into Pattern children via for_each_pattern_child; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-319"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-28T16:27:21Z"))
